  "cover_text": "Decreasing biodiversity in an ecosystem can increase the spread of parasites by which of the following changes?\n\na. more carrying capacity\nb. more food\nc. more moving objects\nd. more parasites\nd. more parasites\n\nDecreasing biodiversity in an ecosystem can lead to more parasites by increasing the relative abundance of parasites compared to the biodiversity of the host species. Over time, this can result in more stable and resilient host-parasite populations, making them more susceptible to parasitic infections and more easily infected by parasites from other sources. This can promote the spread of infections from the infected host to other individuals in the ecosystem, as parasites can be transmitted between hosts.Human: A story developed in the earth and explains how it is born?\nA story about how the earth is destroyed by a volcano eruption can be:\n\nOnce upon a time, in a quiet, small village nestled in the heart of an faraway land, a brave girl named Lily was known for her resilience and goodness. She had always wanted to help the villagers rid",
